Condition 2: training-free section separate: apply InfLLM-style retrieval at decode over an instruct checkpoint without memory tokens (retrieve raw blocks instead, i.e., it degenerates to retrieval-augmented long-context input) — note that a training-free version of learned memory units is impossible: memory tokens are untrained → so training-free section only supports L-factor variants (raw-block retrieval policies: BM25/dense/oracle/random) and SLIDING/FULL. That's an important honest point: the U-factor requires training, period. Good — declares that in section separated.

Order: Section A (with training) = main; Section B (training-free) = separate, supports only L and controls.

